00:00:57.816 --> 00:00:59.940
Well I think what I struggle
with with in my business,

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.420
so I created a specializing
booking platform

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:06.470
specific to working with group bookings.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.902
I think where I got a
little confused in where,

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.580
like the growth of the business,

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.974
I find that because
we're a service business

00:01:12.974 --> 00:01:15.430
I run into where I kind of either plateau

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:19.420
or it's I can't hire fast
enough for the demand.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.610
So then I just am like
kind of a sitting duck

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:24.160
and trying to chase, hiring more artists,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.100
which becomes like management

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.446
like we just kind of bottle neck.

00:01:27.446 --> 00:01:31.310
- So on that as somebody who
scaled a service business

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.883
is it hiring or is it retaining?

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.450
- It's hiring.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:40.183
- And are you making
subjective calls when you hire?

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.340
- How so?

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.470
- Are you the one hiring?

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.140
- Yeah, I'm a part of the process, yeah.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.150
- Right, so the way I ask the question

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.610
is the most important part.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.680
I think most people struggle with hiring

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.500
because they come from a angle of fear

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.350
and when they look at hiring
they're thinking about

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:00.850
what they're trying to protect against

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.720
because you think that
person or this person

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.620
or that person is representing
you in this environment

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:07.130
and you don't want them to fuck up

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.730
in however you deem it.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.408
You're coming from fear.

00:02:10.408 --> 00:02:13.210
The reason I think I've been
able to scale two businesses

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.656
so quickly in my life is I'm the reverse.

00:02:15.656 --> 00:02:19.010
I always think that if my intent is good

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:22.713
that by hiring quickly
I can actually scale

00:02:22.713 --> 00:02:26.440
and that in the occasional 20% of time

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.810
when it's really actually fucked up,

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.464
my ability to fix it
out of intent and effort

00:02:32.464 --> 00:02:35.344
is actually greater
than me judging upfront

00:02:35.344 --> 00:02:37.230
and not hiring at all.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:40.870
- So my fear what that is that
my typical client is a bride.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.703
- Yep.

00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:43.590
- Or a large corporate booking

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.410
and so like reputation
wise, like you get one shot.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.730
- But you don't.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.500
- With that particular client.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.030
- You're not gonna see another bride again

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.670
most likely anyway.
- Right.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.810
- And you would lose her word of mouth

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.700
and her word of mouth is only so impactful

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.240
but what you lose for is
you're not doing and scaling

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.943
out of the fear that maybe it goes poorly.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.760
What most people struggle
with in business is

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.317
they spend all their time
on what's gonna go wrong

00:03:11.317 --> 00:03:13.597
instead of what's gonna go right.

00:03:13.597 --> 00:03:17.329
So yeah, big clients and brides I get it.

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:21.330
Good news brides don't
have great LTV, right?

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.457
And good news seven out of 10 time,

00:03:24.457 --> 00:03:26.590
it's gonna be perfectly fine.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:27.423
- Yeah.

00:03:27.423 --> 00:03:30.503
- And good news you've hired
people that fucked up anyway.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.137
So where I'm going with all this is

00:03:35.137 --> 00:03:38.475
you need to hire quicker

00:03:38.475 --> 00:03:42.080
and be more optimistic versus pessimistic.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.470
- I think I get worried where

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.180
it's the management of both sides

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.320
and so like I built my
own booking platform

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.150
to help streamline that management

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:50.900
and then what I found is that

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:53.240
many other similar business models

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:55.360
that are like across the
country are struggling

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.280
with the same pain point

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.880
with not having the
right management system,

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.820
where I was able to build that,

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.377
so my question was do I
hit pivot a little or stay?

00:04:02.377 --> 00:04:05.181
- And what, become a SAS business?

00:04:05.181 --> 00:04:06.513
Which is fine.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.703
You could, do you want to?

00:04:10.576 --> 00:04:11.978
- I don't know.

00:04:11.978 --> 00:04:14.220
- Well that's what you need to figure out,

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.280
but I will tell you that on the other side

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.081
of your service business,

00:04:18.081 --> 00:04:20.810
it's been the clearest thing for me.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:22.330
It was my hypothesis going in,

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.060
it's my natural state,

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.010
people spend all their time on defense.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:30.780
What if Carl fucks up
this wedding, instead of

00:04:32.791 --> 00:04:34.760
not thinking that,

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.300
which then leads you to hiring Carl

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.283
instead of not hiring him

00:04:38.283 --> 00:04:40.490
because he answered one question in a way

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:43.397
that maybe you as a human
subjectively thought

00:04:43.397 --> 00:04:45.832
would lead to a vulnerability.

00:04:45.832 --> 00:04:47.670
- Well it's usually on the talent level.

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:50.340
It's just like the quality
of what they're able to do.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.180
- Yeah, but you're making
that subjective call.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:55.590
What you might think
is good may or may not,

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:58.180
I mean you've had plenty of
brides tell you this is shit

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.003
when you thought it was
great and vice versa.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:04.990
Right?

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:08.060
I mean it's a super important
part of this question,

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:11.330
like you may decide that
I'm not qualified enough

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:15.080
but you're making a judgment
for the market without knowing.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.260
The reason you're not hiring fast enough

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:18.160
is because of you.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.183
Your subjective call.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:26.890
- Not always but--

00:05:27.935 --> 00:05:29.490
